WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.910
Off Ireland's west coast,
on the island of Inis Mor,

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.870
a monk called Enda built a monastery.

3
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.160
Others followed.

4
00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.830
Finnian at Clonard.

5
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.470
Brigit at Kildare.

6
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.110
Brendan at Clonfert.

7
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.270
And more.

8
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.700
Their monks fasted, prayed
with arms outstretched,

9
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.630
and some even stood in cold water.

10
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.390
Across much of Europe, bishops
in towns led the Church.

11
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:29.010
So why did Ireland's church come
to be led by abbots in monasteries?

12
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:33.250
In this mission, you'll meet five
founders and the monasteries they built.

13
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.260
Then you'll weigh up two historians' views
of how complete the change really was.

14
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:43.000
Your mission: explain why Ireland's
church came to be led by abbots.
